    "title": "Average delay",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-17T13:07:00Z",
    "description": "<p data-renderer-start-pos=\"4731\">For the given set of filter data (i.e. date range, granularity (hour, day, or month), operator and line), the query will return:</p><p data-renderer-start-pos=\"4861\"><strong>scheduled_departures:</strong> total number of scheduled stop departures</p><p data-renderer-start-pos=\"4944\"><strong>total_departures:</strong> total number of actual stop departures observed</p><p data-renderer-start-pos=\"5011\"><strong>total_delay:</strong> sum of differences between actual and scheduled departure times (in seconds).</p><p data-renderer-start-pos=\"5103\">We can then formulate the average delay = <strong>total_delay / total_departures</strong></p>",
    "description_text": "For the given set of filter data (i.e. date range, granularity (hour, day, or month), operator and line), the query will return: scheduled_departures: total number of scheduled stop departures total_departures: total number of actual stop departures observed total_delay: sum of differences between actual and scheduled departure times (in seconds). We can then formulate the average delay = total_delay / total_departures",
